  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><msub><mi>Og</mi><mn>118</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>8</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is&nbsp;the configuration for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn></math>.</p><p>Since the differentiating electron is entering in the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>-</mo></math>orbital, the element will belong to the s-block and the outermost s-orbital is having two electrons. Hence, It will belong to the alkaline earth metal&nbsp;group.</p>",
